# Train 5: p5-mcp-discover-stdio-modern with the OSC 7501 wire taken as it goes: at
# launch with the server starting, once its startup is over, after `/mcp show`, after
# the turn that calls its tool, and after `/quit`. What the program status says while an
# MCP server starts in the 2026-07-28 era, on fx and on xfx. A scratch copy, not a
# scenario of the repository. The rest is the twin's:
# p5 mcp discover: a 2026-07-28 stdio server (p5-mcp-discover-stdio.ts `modern`). fx
# v0.0.16 asks `server/discover` first (src/mcp/core/era.zig@481104fd), the server lists
# 2026-07-28, and it is served in that era: no `initialize`, and every request carries the
# 2026 `_meta`, which the fixture insists on. `/mcp show` says the version; one turn
# searches and calls its tool twice; `home wire` is what the server was sent.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-modern-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-modern-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-turns.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=full-access
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
# The full-access warning is up from the first frame for 4 s (capfile.py
# TIMERS): `/mcp show` is typed once it has come and gone, so its `/` does
# not take the warning's row and stop its clock (train 4, as FLAKE-HINT4's
# p5-mcp-turn).
until shown Full access
wire m00-start
wait 6
until gone Full access
wire m01-started
type /mcp show fixture
key Enter
wait 3
snap show
wire m02-show
type use the fixture echo tool
key Enter
wait 12
snap turn
wire m03-turn
home wire
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
wire m04-exit
